# Computational interpretation notebook — {{ project_name }}

This append-only notebook records **human interpretation of registered
computational executions**. It does not replace either current generated
`results/provenance.json`, the append-only `metadata/runs.csv` index, or the
immutable `metadata/provenance/<execution_id>.json` archive.

Workflow:

```bash
# 1. Human approves durable registration of the current generated run.
python scripts/register_run.py "short factual note"

# 2. After registration succeeds, generate an entry stub and have a person
#    complete objective, outcome, limitations, and interpretation.
python scripts/lab_notebook_entry.py >> reporting/writeups/LAB_NOTEBOOK.md
```

Each entry must name an execution ID already present in `metadata/runs.csv` and
must agree with its archived provenance. Machine facts are retrieved, never
typed from memory. A person owns the objective, observations about what worked or
failed, limitations, biological/statistical interpretation, and follow-up
decision. Agents may draft from supplied evidence but may not append/accept an
interpretation without explicit approval.

Do not rewrite earlier entries. Correct an error with a new dated amendment that
references the original execution and entry.

